message.content:
{
  "text": "The tutors language model employs a decoder only transformer to process text. A tokenizer divides an input passage into tokens. An embedding layer maps these tokens to numerical vectors. Positional information helps the transformer distinguish sequences containing the same tokens in different orders. Self attention combines information from token representations. A causal attention mask prevents the model from attending to later positions when predicting the next token. Attention connects information across a passage, though models have a finite context window that limits the text available in a single request. Restrictions apply to both training and generation phases. Attention weights do not validate the truth of associated claims.",
  "reason": "The reconstruction follows the source occurrence order of relations provided in the data. Each relation is mapped directly: 'employs_component_for' links the model to its architecture; 'divides' and 'maps' describe the preprocessing pipeline; 'helps' explains the role of positional info; 'combines' describes self-attention mechanics; 'prevents' details the causal mask constraint during prediction; 'applies_to' covers restrictions on training/generation; 'connects' describes attention's function with its modality ('can'); 'limits' addresses the context window constraint; and 'validates_claim' is negated per its modality ('does not'). All participant roles, conditions (e.g., 'when predicting next token'), and argument qualifiers are preserved without inference."
}

